NabuGpuMemoryPolicy.h and the NativeAdrenoMemory.h allocation overload select
Normal-NC owned user BOs only when NABU_GPU_METAL=1. The original seven-argument
allocator remains unchanged: write_combined=true bypasses its WB pool, chooses
kIOMapWriteCombineCache and records NC physical spans. Existing prepared-backing
reuse still matches the cache mode. Explicit cache-mode calls and imported pages
retain their old behavior; no A642L cached-coherence gate is enabled.
NativeAdrenoGpuContext.cpp gives Metal the VM's existing 4096-record bound, not
the 16-record diagnostic pool. This allocates only CPU mapping/alias metadata at
attach, not backing BOs or additional GPU page tables. Allocation failure remains
fatal to bring-up. A Metal-only static assertion in NativeAdrenoVm.cpp bounds the
two attach-time arrays to 1 MiB using their actual compiled element sizes. The
diagnostic capacity and five bootstrap mappings are unchanged.
These source changes do not qualify BO mapping, completion or rendering on hardware.
